\taxon{Example}
\title{A rational motor checks every projective coordinate layer}

\p{Take

##{c=\frac35,\qquad s=\frac45,\qquad t=(4,0).}

Then

##{U=\frac{3-4e_{12}}5,\qquad
R_U=\frac1{25}\begin{pmatrix}-7&-24\\24&-7\end{pmatrix},}

and the ordered motor is

##{M=T(4,0)U
=\frac35-\frac45e_{12}-\frac85e_{20}-\frac65e_{01}.}

Its full named tuple and the ascending core tuple supplied by
\ref{fcap-002R} are

##{\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{named}(M)
 &=\left(\frac35,0,0,0,-\frac45,-\frac85,-\frac65,0\right),\\
\operatorname{core}(M)
 &=\left(\frac35,0,0,-\frac65,0,\frac85,-\frac45,0\right).
\end{aligned}}

Thus the calculation enters the algebra through all eight-coordinate
conversion data, including the #{e_{20}=-e_{02}} sign.}

\p{The point and line

##{P_0=P(1,3,-1),\qquad L_0=L(3,-1,0)}

are incident. The motor action gives

##{\begin{aligned}
MP_0M^{-1}&=P\left(1,\frac{103}{25},\frac{79}{25}\right),\\
ML_0M^{-1}&=L\left(\frac{47}{25},\frac7{25},-\frac{24}{25}\right).
\end{aligned}}

The output incidence check is

##{\frac{47}{25}
 +\frac7{25}\frac{103}{25}
 -\frac{24}{25}\frac{79}{25}=0.}

The output point has tuples

##{\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{named}(MP_0M^{-1})
 &=\left(0,0,0,0,1,\frac{103}{25},\frac{79}{25},0\right),\\
\operatorname{core}(MP_0M^{-1})
 &=\left(0,0,0,\frac{79}{25},0,-\frac{103}{25},1,0\right).
\end{aligned}}

This checks the geometric action and the signed coordinate adapter on the
same exact example.}

\p{Reversal gives the algebra inverse, and sandwiching the two outputs by
#{\widetilde M} and #{M} returns both original representatives. In the same
ordered factorization,

##{M^{-1}=M\left(\left(\frac{28}{25},\frac{96}{25}\right),U^{-1}\right).}

Composition order is visible: reversing the factors gives

##{UT(4,0):P(1,3,-1)\longmapsto P(1,-1,7),}

which differs from the output above. These are exact rational identities,
not floating-point or private-software evidence. FCAP does not yet expose the
named executable product and conversion theorems needed to certify this
calculation as a public implementation refinement.}
